      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name}\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nI understand regarding the log file.\n\nHowever, since the issue in my environment occurred quite some time ago and my memory is somewhat vague,I will collect and send several logs from around the time when the issue likely occurred.\n\nPlease also excuse me for extracting and sending only the relevant portion (from leaving the previous instance until closing VRC),in order to protect my friends’ privacy.\n\nIf necessary, I can send the entire file as-is, but in that case, I would appreciate it if you could suggest a method of transfer that is not publicly accessible.\n\nI am aware that there is a feature where, if you are kicked from a world, you cannot rejoin that instance for a certain period of time.\n\n(My memory is a bit hazy, but as far as I remember from when I was an event staff member, being kicked by an instance master prevented rejoining for at least about an hour.)\n\nThat said, I would like to clarify that when this issue occurred, the first error message I saw (displayed in the game’s UI) was a warning from EAC.\n\nTherefore, I understand that it was not caused by a kick from within the instance.\n\n(After taking countermeasures, I was able to rejoin the same instance within about 30 minutes.)\n\nIf the behavior when being disconnected due to an EAC error is the same as when being kicked, I have no particular concerns.\n\nHowever, if my memory is correct, I recall that the handling was different, which makes me wonder if this might be another issue — specifically, that you cannot return to the instance afterward.\n\nRegarding the “black screen,” as far as I remember, on desktop it often remains completely black,but in VR, it wasn’t a total “black screen” — I could still see something resembling the world.\n\nTherefore, it seems that the “black screen” occurs during the situation described in section 4.B above.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
